*Step 1: Contact both parties*

* Take the driver’s and rider’s contact information from the ticket to call them. If they don’t respond, try calling them again in 5 minutes. If you cannot reach them after the 3rd attempt, inform your Team Lead. 
** The ticket is connected to the driver’s profile, so you can call them from the ticket
** For the rider’s phone number, take the rider ID from the order details and [+create a ticket+|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360011272234--Creating-a-New-Ticket-in-Zendesk] to their ZD profile to call them.
* Advise them that the vehicle hasn’t moved for a while and you’re just checking if everything is alright. Add any information you receive to the internal notes of the ZD ticket.
** If both parties responded to the call and confirmed that they’re okay, close the initial ticket
** If only the rider/driver responded and confirmed they’re okay, continue contacting the other party
** If they confirm that there is an issue that falls under High Priority, continue with the next step. If it’s not a High Priority case, follow the correct [+internal process+|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/categories/360000688773-Ride-hailing] to solve the case.

